cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "QOV: virus and prophage identification in human gut metagenome assemblies"
message: "If you use this software, please cite the accompanying manuscript."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Valenzuela-Diaz
    given-names: Sandro
    email: sandrolvalenzuelad@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/questomics/QOVirome"
url: "https://questomics.app"
abstract: >-
  QOV identifies viral and prophage sequences in human gut metagenome assemblies. A permissive
  union of detection tools gathers candidate sequence, and a single supervised model over 176
  features - combining measured evidence (gene census, protein profile hits, viral-versus-cellular
  homology contrast, marker scores) with learned prediction (neural composition models and raw
  tetranucleotide frequencies) - decides admission. The pipeline is distributed as one
  self-contained Apptainer image with every database baked in.
keywords:
  - virome
  - bacteriophage
  - prophage
  - metagenomics
  - human gut microbiome
  - machine learning
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-12"
